<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cultural Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1966">1966</a>–<a href="/years/1976">1976</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Great Proletarian Cultural Revolution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cultural Revolution was a political campaign launched by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in 1966 to reassert his authority and purge the Communist Party of supposed capitalist and traditional elements. Students organised as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-guards-china">Red Guards</a> attacked officials, teachers and 'old' culture, and leaders such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-shaoqi">Liu Shaoqi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deng-xiaoping">Deng Xiaoping</a> were purged. Hundreds of thousands, perhaps millions, died. It ended with Mao's death and the arrest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gang-of-four">Gang of Four</a> in 1976.</p></div>
